From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiron Builder <builder@chiron.local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 19:48:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/44] media: vrr, sound: leave the hardware alone on halt and
 power-off too

The vendor shutdown callbacks only skipped their teardown when the machine
was restarting. On halt and power-off they still tried to talk to hardware
whose clocks the same shutdown sequence had already taken away, which is
where the board was seen to hang instead of powering down.

Validated on this board;
the rest of that patch is already in this queue.
---
 drivers/media/vrr/vrr_drv.c   | 4 +++-
 sound/soc/amlogic/auge/card.c | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/vrr/vrr_drv.c b/drivers/media/vrr/vrr_drv.c
index 1362a76c0..6cb65be3d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/vrr/vrr_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vrr/vrr_drv.c
@@ -1490,7 +1490,9 @@ static void vrr_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct aml_vrr_drv_s *vdrv = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART)
+	if (system_state == SYSTEM_HALT ||
+	    system_state == SYSTEM_POWER_OFF ||
+	    system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART)
 		return;
 
 	if (vdrv->sw_timer_flag) {
diff --git a/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/card.c b/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/card.c
index 1222e7e6a..58a8e7ddd 100644
--- a/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/card.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/card.c
@@ -1640,7 +1640,9 @@ static void aml_card_platform_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct snd_soc_card *card = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct aml_card_data *priv = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(card);
 
-	if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART)
+	if (system_state == SYSTEM_HALT ||
+	    system_state == SYSTEM_POWER_OFF ||
+	    system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART)
 		goto stop_thread;
 
 	priv->av_mute_enable = 1;
